              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marwadi for medicine, then the Marwadi for hunger."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: राजी",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "राजी — rājī — \"happy, content\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "राजी (rājī) is a loan from Arabic rāḍī, \"content, pleased\", which reached Marwadi through Persian. Its Arabic root is r-ḍ-w (Lane). Persian says it rāzī; Marwadi says the z as j."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
